{"id":165,"date":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/localhost:8181\/duplex-peace-treaty-separate-comfort-for-beaver-falls-two-family-homes\/"},"modified":"2026-07-14T19:43:56","modified_gmt":"2026-07-14T19:43:56","slug":"duplex-peace-treaty-separate-comfort-for-beaver-falls-two-family-homes","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/duplex-peace-treaty-separate-comfort-for-beaver-falls-two-family-homes\/","title":{"rendered":"Beaver Falls Sits in a Bowl of Trapped Air\u2014Your HVAC Feels It"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover alignfull s-hero-cover\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:2rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:2rem\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim-70 has-background-dim\"><\/span><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-194\" alt=\"wood stove fire interior\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/6065540454_7be71d4c0a_b.jpg\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/6065540454_7be71d4c0a_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/6065540454_7be71d4c0a_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/6065540454_7be71d4c0a_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-cover-is-layout-ff0c90b8 wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center has-base-color has-text-color s-hero-cover__title wp-block-heading\">Valley cold traps your comfort<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center s-lead has-base-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">The Beaver River valley creates temperature inversions and humidity conditions that standard HVAC systems can&#039;t address alone.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Schedule the Walkthrough<\/a><\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"#content\">Learn More<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"s-trust-bar\"><div class=\"s-trust__item\">15+ Years Serving PA<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Licensed &amp; Insured<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Same-Day Emergency<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Local to Your Area<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-overlap has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-10371125 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-overlap__img has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large alignwide\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2.png\" alt=\"furnace - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1758\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-furnace-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-overlap__card has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-bfed0f9d wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:2.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:2.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How valley inversions kill heating efficiency<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Temperature inversions occur when cold air settles into low-lying areas and gets trapped by surrounding topography. In Beaver Falls, this happens on clear, calm nights when radiational cooling produces cold air that flows downslope into the river valley and pools there.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Valley-bottom homes on Seventh Avenue, Tenth Street, and Patterson Heights neighborhoods experience outdoor temperatures five to ten degrees colder than properties on hillsides just a few hundred feet higher, while simultaneously dealing with higher humidity from river moisture and fog formation.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For heating systems, these inversion conditions create two specific problems: higher heat loss from larger temperature differentials between inside and outside, and increased infiltration of cold, humid air requiring more energy to condition. A furnace maintaining sixty-eight degrees when it&#039;s twenty-five outside has a forty-three degree differential\u2014but in a valley inversion where ground-level temperature is fifteen degrees, the differential jumps to fifty-three degrees.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat loss through walls, windows, and foundations increases proportionally, and furnaces run longer and cycle more frequently. Over the heating season, valley location adds ten to fifteen percent to energy costs compared to identical homes at higher elevations.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--cream has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Moisture control as a separate system<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Valley homes experience both external moisture from air infiltration and internal moisture from occupancy, cooking, and bathing. The dehumidification capacity needs to handle both sources during peak humidity periods. A system sized only for internal loads will struggle when valley fog brings infiltration moisture loads that are two or three times higher than standard residential assumptions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Whole-house dehumidification integrated with forced air heating treats humidity as a controlled parameter just like temperature. Ducted systems use existing ductwork to condition air from the entire house, maintaining target humidity levels automatically while dumping condensate to a drain.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Integrating dehumidification control with heating\u2014so the fan operates even when heat isn&#039;t needed\u2014allows moisture removal independent of temperature demand, and dry air feels warmer at the same temperature, allowing setpoint reductions of two to three degrees without comfort loss.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--ink has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Air filtration for humidity-heavy environments<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">High humidity in valley locations creates conditions where mold spores, dust mites, and biological contaminants thrive. Standard fiberglass furnace filters with MERV 1-4 ratings protect equipment but don&#039;t improve air quality. Upgrading to pleated media filters with MERV 8-13 ratings captures these particles effectively\u2014if filters are changed on schedule and the duct system is tight enough that air flows through rather than bypassing around the frame.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-icon-list\">\n<li>Filter fit and sealing matter as much as rating\u2014a MERV 13 filter that allows bypass provides no benefit. Proper installation with weather stripping around the frame ensures all return air passes through media.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Electronic air cleaners and activated-carbon media address odors and chemical contaminants that standard filtration misses, including musty smells from mold growth and volatile organic compounds from building materials.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>UV-C germicidal lights in ductwork or near evaporator coils reduce mold and bacterial growth on cooling coils and drain pans where moisture accumulates. UV lamps prevent these areas from becoming sources of biological contamination distributed through the house.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Filter maintenance intervals need to be shorter in valley homes\u2014moisture accelerates particle loading and can cause filter media to break down. A filter lasting three months in typical Pennsylvania homes might need replacement every six to eight weeks in damp valley environments.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Duct cleaning provides temporary improvement in homes where years of humidity caused mold and dust accumulation, but it&#039;s not a substitute for ongoing filtration and moisture control. Cleaned ducts recontaminate within months if moisture conditions aren&#039;t addressed.<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--warm-gradient has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Beaver Falls valley HVAC services<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-cards-3 is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-card--accent is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Moisture assessments<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Diagnose basement and crawlspace moisture sources, evaluate infiltration paths, and determine dehumidification requirements for your valley location.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-card--accent is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Integrated dehumidification<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Install whole-house dehumidifiers that coordinate with heating systems, use existing ductwork, and maintain humidity independent of temperature demand.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-card--accent is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ductwork sealing<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Seal ductwork gaps and connections in basements and crawlspaces to prevent condensation, heat loss, and humid air bypass that defeats filtration.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-card--accent is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Foundation vapor control<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Install crawlspace barriers and foundation wall vapor retardation to reduce soil moisture transmission and prevent humid basement air from entering living spaces.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-card--accent is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">High-efficiency filtration<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Upgrade to MERV 8-13 filters, install activated-carbon media for odor control, and add UV germicidal lighting for biological contamination management.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-card--accent is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ventilation optimization<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Design heat recovery or energy recovery ventilation systems that provide controlled fresh air without excessive energy loss or humidity penalties in cold valley microclimates.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why valley homes are different<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Living in the Beaver River valley means accepting that your home operates in a microclimate that differs substantially from regional weather reports and standard HVAC design assumptions. The fog that settles overnight, the cold air pooling at street level, and the dampness persisting through morning are not occasional weather events but predictable geographic realities that repeat through the heating season and affect comfort regardless of furnace performance.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">College Hill homes between Seventh and Thirteenth Street\u2014mostly duplexes and older residences converted from coal to gas in the sixties\u2014still run furnaces from that era, pushing heated air through original tin ductwork with gaps at every joint, spiking Penn Power bills and leaving cold spots in every back bedroom.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-diagnostic has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-b267b866 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:3rem\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Valley-home moisture red flags<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Basement walls damp to the touch below grade\u2014cold-air pooling driving condensation on cool surfaces<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Morning fog inside lower-level windows\u2014exterior dew point exceeding interior surface temperature<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Dehumidifier running continuously May-September\u2014foundation infiltration exceeding unit capacity<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Ductwork in basement showing surface rust\u2014condensation from temperature differential between basement and supply air<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Mold or mildew at floor level in finished basement\u2014moisture barrier inadequate or absent<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--dark-gradient has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-stats is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">10-15%<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Higher heating costs in valley vs. hilltop locations<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">5-10\u00b0F<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Temperature difference between valley floor and nearby hillsides during inversions<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">2-3x<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Moisture infiltration during fog periods compared to standard residential design assumptions<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">70-80%<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Heat recovery efficiency with ERV systems for controlled ventilation<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Valley climate HVAC questions<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-accordion s-accordion--bordered has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1583283a wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Why does my home feel damp even when the heat is running?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heating raises air temperature but doesn&#039;t remove moisture, so humid air that infiltrates from outside or generates from indoor sources feels clammy despite adequate temperature. Whole-house dehumidification integrated with your heating system addresses moisture as a separate control parameter, maintaining comfortable humidity levels regardless of heating demand.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Do valley homes need different HVAC equipment than homes at higher elevations?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Valley locations benefit from integrated moisture control (dehumidification or ERV systems), higher-efficiency filtration to address biological contaminants that thrive in humidity, and properly sized heating equipment accounting for colder outdoor temperatures that inversions create. Standard equipment can work, but system design should address microclimate conditions specific to valley geography.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>How much does valley location affect heating costs?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Temperature inversions and higher humidity can increase heating costs ten to fifteen percent compared to similar homes at higher elevations, due to colder outdoor air during inversions and the energy required to warm humid infiltration air. Proper air sealing, insulation, and moisture control reduce but don&#039;t eliminate the geographic penalty that valley locations experience.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>What&#039;s the best way to fix cold spots in valley homes?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The fix is usually in the ductwork, not the furnace. Original tin ductwork from coal-to-gas conversions in sixties-era College Hill homes has gaps at every joint, allowing heated air to leak before reaching distant rooms. Sealing ductwork and right-sizing equipment to valley heating loads eliminates cold spots and reduces energy waste.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Is basement dehumidification worth the cost?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Yes, especially in valley locations where foundation moisture is continuous rather than seasonal. Basement dehumidification protects ductwork from corrosion, prevents mold growth that infiltrates living spaces, and allows right-sized dehumidification upstairs rather than equipment fighting continuous moisture influx from below.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Our Work in Your Neighborhood<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery alignwide has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped s-gallery wp-block-gallery-2 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" data-id=\"1755\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1755\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" data-id=\"193\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/34009503281_9a1243133e_b.jpg\" alt=\"wood stove fire interior\" class=\"wp-image-193\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/34009503281_9a1243133e_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/34009503281_9a1243133e_b-300x200.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/34009503281_9a1243133e_b-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;An old tile stove&quot; by freestocks.org, CC0, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" data-id=\"179\" src=\"\/wp-content\/